      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "# Nexus-7 Proximity Sensor Quick-Start Guide\n## Power & Connection\n- **Power Input**: Connect 5V DC via USB-C cable.\n- **Connection Check**: Verify solid green LED indicates active power.\n## System Setup\n- **Terminal Access**: Open terminal and type 'nexus-sync'.\n- **Sync Verification**: Wait for blinking green LED during sync.\n- **Final Status**: Confirm solid green LED for active operation.\n## Calibration Procedure\n- **Surface Prep**: Ensure flat surface is clean and dry.\n- **Distance Check**: Hold sensor exactly 10cm from surface.\n- **Button Action**: Press 'Calibrate' button for 3 seconds.\n## Safety Protocols\n- **Liquid Warning**: Never submerge sensor in any liquid.\n- **Voltage Limit**: Strictly avoid exceeding 5V input.\n- **UV Warning**: Avoid high-intensity UV during calibration.\n## Mounting Instructions\n- **Hardware Prep**: Select M3 screw for standard bracket.\n- **Installation**: Secure sensor firmly into bracket.\n- **Final Check**: Verify all connections before use.",
